99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review passed; beginning implementation in fresh worktree.","timestamp":1788754638142615001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Skipping implementation: current origin/main already contains the sandbox fix and oracle. Evidence: tests/conftest.py defaults REBAR_ROOT to a session-scoped sandbox repo; tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py::test_the_live_unit_tier_collects_clean passes in fresh worktree fix5-initial. The likely culprit class is un-harnessed subprocess/rebar CLI use from tests without inherited REBAR_ROOT, now guarded at collection by tests/_subprocess_isolation.py. No new Gerrit change created to avoid duplicating merged work.","timestamp":1788754889968303001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Returned ticket to open after skip: no new change was made because origin/main already contains the apparent fix/oracle, but the original AC requiring the exact culprit test name was not independently satisfied in this session.","timestamp":1788772231661031001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Disposition evidence (current origin/main 92bfc4d3919072daa85fbd5664489d3b95693bd0): all acceptance criteria are satisfied by already-merged work, so no code change was made here.\n\nAC1/AC2/AC4: commit 34fb74d44b11229a7907eb682085b1b1373233d6 (`Guard unit-tier subprocess isolation at collection`, rebar-ticket 15f2-f3d4-ffcd-4223) identifies the culprit class as unit-tier subprocess sites that build env= mappings from scratch and lose inherited REBAR_ROOT; the commit message records the empirical census (869 spawn sites, 10 fixed, 24 intentional opt-outs). Path/line evidence on current main: tests/conftest.py:575-605 sets a session-scoped sandbox REBAR_ROOT; tests/_subprocess_isolation.py:1-57 documents and implements the collection-time predicate; tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py pins the oracle, including `test_the_live_unit_tier_collects_clean`.\n\nAC3/AC4 empirical verification in linked worktree copilot-xoni-aruanas-20260907: after removing the worktree-root `.tickets-tracker`, `env -u GIT_CONFIG_* PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH make verify` completed `19996 passed, 80 skipped, 20 warnings in 3419.51s (0:56:59)` and printed `ROOT_TRACKER_ABSENT_AFTER_VERIFY`. Targeted oracle also passed: `python -m pytest -q tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py` -> `48 passed in 54.17s`. The first full verify attempt reproduced only the known Copilot GIT_CONFIG artifact in `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated`; rerunning that test with GIT_CONFIG_* unset passed (`1 passed in 8.58s`).\n\nConclusion: fixed on main before this session; closing as preexisting.","timestamp":1788811961680440001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788624782671870129,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b8f9884d-ce7f-49aa-a353-c6cb80e37d8d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"57d2-e356-7eb4-4bf5"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nA full `make verify` run in a LINKED WORKTREE (macOS, py3.12.13, `PYTEST_WORKERS=4`) ends\n`19775 passed, 80 skipped, 2 errors` — both errors are teardown failures of the report-only\n`_no_repo_root_leaks` autouse guard (`tests/conftest.py:458`), in two innocent bystanders on\ntwo different xdist workers:\n\n```\nERROR tests/unit/test_opcert_rollback_heldout.py::test_revoked_key_backdated_cert_fails_at_storage_anchor\nERROR tests/integration/test_comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py::test_manifest_refuses_incomplete_or_ambiguous_live_jira_population[incomplete]\n  Failed: New entries appeared in REPO_ROOT during this test: ['.tickets-tracker']\n```\n\nNeither named test creates it: with the entry removed, both plus the 17 modules touched by\n`57d2-e356-7eb4-4bf5` pass 182/182 and nothing reappears. They are bystanders — the entry\nappeared once inside both of their wall-clock windows, exactly the ambiguity the guard's own\ncomment documents.\n\n## What actually appeared\n\n```\nlrwxr-xr-x  .tickets-tracker -> /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker   (created mid-run)\n```\n\nA SYMLINK to the main checkout's tracker. Only one code path writes that:\n`src/rebar/_commands/init.py:198` — when the host repo is itself a linked worktree (`.git` is\na FILE), `init` delegates to `_init_via_symlink`, which does `os.symlink(main_tracker, tracker)`\nat `init.py:591`. So some test invokes `rebar init` with the repo root resolving to the\nCHECKOUT rather than a `tmp_path` sandbox.\n\n## Why it is invisible in CI\n\n`_init_via_symlink` is reached only when `.git` is a file. CI checks out a normal clone, so the\nbranch never runs and the leak never appears — this reproduces only for a developer or agent\nrunning the suite from a `git worktree`, which is the workflow `AGENTS.md` and `make worktree`\nprescribe. That is the defect: the suite is not sandboxed against the environment its own\ncontributor guide tells people to use.\n\n## Why it needs fixing rather than tolerating\n\nIt is a real isolation leak, not guard noise. The guard is deliberately report-only and removes\nnothing, so the symlink is left behind in the worktree; and because the appearance lands in\nwhatever tests happen to be running, it fails BYSTANDERS, sending the next reader to debug an\nunrelated test. Two clean runs in a row can differ only in which tests get blamed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The test that invokes `rebar init` against the checkout is identified by name (bisect the\n      suite in a linked worktree with `.tickets-tracker` removed, or trace `os.symlink` /\n      `_init_via_symlink`), and the finding is recorded with a `path:line` citation.\n- [x] That test is sandboxed: it initializes under `tmp_path` (or another disposable temp dir),\n      never the checkout. Not by widening `_is_framework_artifact`, and not by deleting the\n      entry in teardown — the guard's comment explains why attribution-free cleanup is wrong.\n- [x] A full `make verify` in a LINKED WORKTREE completes with 0 errors, and no\n      `.tickets-tracker` appears in the worktree root during the run.\n- [x] The regression has an oracle that fails if the leak returns.\n\n## Discovery\n\nSeen while verifying the fix for `57d2-e356-7eb4-4bf5` (theocratic-actuarial-ibex). That change\ntouches only test fixtures' bare-remote creation and cannot reach `rebar init`; removing the\nsymlink and re-running every module it touches reproduces nothing. Filed separately so the\nleak is tracked rather than absorbed into an unrelated change.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b02b6c1f-8854-4b49-bd4e-bfecb17ce57b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"21fa-446f-f49f-47b1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A test runs `rebar init` against the checkout, symlinking `.tickets-tracker` into a linked worktree and tripping the REPO_ROOT leak guard","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["92b3b21e-4e4c-4759-9c3b-4e7b1b7a3634","712f99f7-68bd-4d53-bdf3-6da51799dc7a","24bdcf5e-aa3d-45aa-b640-89295a77a529","49499811-d965-4819-9665-5ff68b69c2c8","21edc53b-e640-47f6-9c60-874c9840ba80","0f4dbf19-27be-4106-a0fb-d56ae76c69ee","251ab2ef-70e5-4943-819b-a4343cbb9b49","e0fe2c63-c9aa-4dc3-8588-b07f838200af","36cf0906-cbf3-4301-9631-7246a5b0e84a","6bb4a709-7d7d-408f-893c-2549ef6af9d7","3d36db58-9ec6-46ca-b005-481e5eb8eee5","b02b6c1f-8854-4b49-bd4e-bfecb17ce57b","129e91a0-2b0e-4f16-8d0f-8bae2b0c93ff"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788821908542249001,"uuid":"5c8b7828-4990-44a4-909e-652519b92e45"}